cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Not All Bad Demonstrations Are Equally Bad: Quantifying How Demonstration Failure Modes Degrade Closed-Loop Policy Performance"
abstract: >-
  A controlled simulation study treating demonstration quality, rather than
  model architecture, as the independent variable. Five demonstration failure
  modes are injected at controlled contamination rates into behaviour-cloning
  datasets for a 2D block-pushing task, and the resulting policies are scored
  with both open-loop action-prediction error and closed-loop task success.
